            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

            <h3>How long is the train from Charlottesville to Burke? </h3>

            <p>The train time from Charlottesville to Burke typically ranges between 1 hour 42 minutes and 1 hour 49 minutes. The Northeast Regional offers direct service on this short regional segment. </p>


            <h3>What is the fastest train from Charlottesville to Burke? </h3>

            <p>The fastest and only option is the Amtrak Northeast Regional, which can complete the journey in approximately 1 hour 42 minutes with direct service. </p>


            <h3>How much does a train cost from Charlottesville to Burke? </h3>

            <p>
                The train from Charlottesville to Burke generally costs between:
                $13 - $25 for advance Saver/Value fares
                $25 - $50 for standard fares
                $50 - $100 for Flexible fares
                $100 - $230+ for business class and last-minute bookings
                Prices vary based on booking timing, fare type, and availability.
            </p>


            <h3>Are there direct trains from Charlottesville to Burke? </h3>

            <p>Yes, the Amtrak Northeast Regional provides direct service without the need for transfers. This is the only direct rail connection between the two cities. </p>


            <h3>Is the Northeast Regional from Charlottesville to Burke worth it? </h3>

            <p>Yes, the Northeast Regional is worth considering for this route due to its affordability, comfort, and direct service. The $13 advance fares make it one of the best values in the Amtrak system. </p>


            <h3>Can you travel from Charlottesville to Burke in one day? </h3>

            <p>Yes, this route is very practical for same-day trips. With a mid-morning departure and short travel time, you can easily travel to Burke and return to Charlottesville the same day using the afternoon northbound service. </p>


            <h3>What is the distance between Charlottesville and Burke by train? </h3>

            <p>The rail distance between Charlottesville and Burke is approximately 84 miles (135 km), making it a short regional rail route in Virginia. </p>


            <h3>Does Burke Centre station have parking? </h3>

            <p>Yes, Burke Centre station has a large multi-level parking garage primarily designed for VRE commuters. Same-day and overnight parking is available for a fee. </p>


            <h3>Can you connect to Washington, D.C. from Burke? </h3>

            <p>Yes, the Virginia Railway Express (VRE) Manassas Line provides weekday commuter service from Burke Centre to Washington Union Station. This connection expands travel options significantly for those heading to the capital. </p>


            <h3>What is the difference between coach and business class? </h3>

            <p>Business class offers more spacious seating, complimentary non-alcoholic beverages, and a quieter environment compared to coach. Both classes have access to the cafe car and free Wi-Fi. On this short route, the difference is modest but noticeable for those prioritizing comfort. </p>


